This internal protocol module derives from the public oauth2 5.0.0 crate by
Alex Crichton, Florin Lipan, David A. Ramos and the upstream contributors.
Original MIT and Apache-2.0 licenses and the exact published source archive
are preserved here. Original notices inside the archive remain unchanged.

The SDK retains OAuth authorization-code/PKCE, refresh, scope checks, client
authentication and the async reqwest transport. Numeric OAuth introspection
instants use time 0.3.55 with checked device-timeout arithmetic. Module paths,
current dependency APIs and compiler lint fixes are recorded in SOURCE.json.
Upstream library documentation is archived, while its original native unit
tests and the SDK's real HTTP callback/refresh tests remain executable in CI.
Transport options never exposed by this SDK (curl/ureq/blocking and plain
PKCE) remain disabled. No existing public SDK feature is removed.

This is private implementation code inside virustotal-rs, with public
crates.io dependencies only. It does not depend on a private Countermeasure
registry or package and introduces no new advisory exception. Replace this
module with the first qualified stable upstream release that removes Chrono
and supports the current HTTP stack, retaining the runtime regressions and
historical source custody.
